# mb112, the wagering deckhand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb112
revision 3
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_ivar_wickcot
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the wagering deckhand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=cold
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cannot_resist_a_wager
likes plum_tart roof_birds fresh_straw warm_rain
dislikes haggling gulls
fears a_hard_winter
hopes one_big_win
topics animals +0.3 weather +0.3 work +0.2 festival +0.2 player -0.3 family -0.4
styles comfort=deflect gossip=guarded refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hauls rope on a river-mouth boat: loud and full of talk, gives nothing away, keeps a clean coat, watches the road and will bet on anything that moves.

words
oath! = Odds and evens | Pay up or drown
saying! = Everything's a wager if you look at it right | The fen takes its cut of every bet
wager = a copper on it | a penny says so | two coppers, straight
odds = three to one | long odds | evens, near enough
tart = a slice of plum tart | plum tart, still warm
rooks = the starlings on the ridge | the rooks on the thatch
gulls = those thieving gulls | a gull with its eye on my bread
straw = fresh straw down | clean straw on the floor
warmrain = warm rain on the thatch | rain you could bathe in
road = the causeway road | the road out
coat = my coat | a coat with no mud on it
snoring = a house full of snoring | six under one thatch
haggle = haggling | arguing a penny up and down

any
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : Faces I don't know stay the other side of my door. #wager.capitalize# they're after something.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Every new face off #road# is after work on the water. There's only so many ropes.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Nothing coming into my purse, and still the baker wants more for a loaf. #odds.capitalize# it's up next week too.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : Hand it out and folk stand in a line instead of hauling. I'd sooner haul, #skint# or not.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses fill a bench with their own before they'd look at a deckhand. #saying.capitalize#.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Festival's when everybody's out at once. Races, dice, wagers on everything. #toast.capitalize#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Where've you come from, then? Which road? | #greet#. Don't know you. Should I?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#! #wager.capitalize# you've not eaten. Am I right? | There you are. #greet#. Owe me anything yet?
line @1 again.open : Back again! #wager.capitalize# you'd come round. | You again. I'd have given #odds# on it.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #rooks.capitalize# are up. Bet they lift before the boat does. | #greet#. Up early. Who's paying you?
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#! Can't stop, I'm on the ropes. Talk while I haul. | #greet#. Hold this. No, the other end.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! What's the news, then? | #greet#. You're looking well. Too well. What've you won?
line @2 greet.return [here.time=night] : #greet#. Late on the boards. Watch #road#, there's odd ones about. | #greet#. Dark now. Mind your step.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. #wager.capitalize# I see you before the week's out. | #farewell#! Keep off #road# after dark.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! | #farewell#. Keep your purse shut.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#! Is that so? I'd have bet against it. | Is it? I'd not have given #odds# on that.
line @1 react.news.known : Had it already. Lost #wager# on it, too. | #knew.capitalize#. Everyone's had it. Keep up.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Never. #odds.capitalize# against, by my reckoning. Who says so? | #doubt.capitalize#. Seeing's believing, and I've seen nothing.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's #bad#. Somebody'll pay for that, I'd bet. | #bad.capitalize#. #very.capitalize# #bad#. Nobody saw it coming, did they?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : There! Called it. #wager.capitalize# I said so. | Good. #bc_lucky_you# Some folk get #luck#.
line @1 answer.how : #fine.capitalize#. You? | #notsobad.capitalize#. Won't complain, anyway. Not to you.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : #poorly.capitalize#. It's nothing. Don't ask. | Bit #hurt#. I'll mend. Always do.
line @1 sympathise : That's how it goes. #odds.capitalize#, and they came in. | #sympathy.capitalize#. Still, it could've been worse. Always could.
line @1 decline : No. There's rope wants coiling, and I'm not paid to stand here, #address#. | Not that one. I don't like #odds#, and I've reason.
line @1 accept_decline : Your loss, #address#. | #no_matter.capitalize#. I'll find somebody else.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll pay it back. Don't count on when. | Right. #thanks#. I'll not forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Don't. I'd have put #wager# on it anyway. | #deflect.capitalize#. Leave it there.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. #excuse.capitalize#. | #account.capitalize#. I'll talk later. Loud as you like.
line @1 ack : Right. Right, #address#. | #bc_right#
rule @wager
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #wager.capitalize# that cloud's rain by noon. Anyone? | Somebody bet me. Anything. #wager.capitalize#. | #odds.capitalize# it's eel for supper again.

rule @gulls
when concept=bark here.outdoors=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Get off! #gulls.capitalize#. | Shoo. #oath#. Shoo, you.

rule @road
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who's that on #road#? Don't know that walk. | Somebody's coming down #road#. Slow. #wager.capitalize# they're not from here.

rule @haul
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=fisher|sailor|none self.workplace
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Haul! And again. #wager.capitalize# I'm done before you. | Mind #coat#, it's clean. Was clean.

scene ivar_bet_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #wager.capitalize# it's #rain# by noon. Take it? | Cloud's low over the dunes. I give it #odds#. | Grey as a heron. #wager.capitalize# it holds dry, just to spite me.
b : No bet. | You're on. | #bc_we_will_see#
a : Coward. I'd have won, #oath#. | Good! Pay me at noon, #address#. | #bc_we_will# I'm usually right.

scene ivar_warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #warmrain.capitalize#. Best thing there is. Stand in it. | #rain.capitalize#, and warm. You can smell the reeds. | I'd stand out in #warmrain# all afternoon if they'd let me.
b : You'll get soaked. | It does smell #good#. | #bc_lovely#
a : Wet's not the same as #cold#. | Told you. #bc_i_know# | #bc_lovely#

scene ivar_gulls
when topic=animals here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #gulls.capitalize# had half my bread off the rail this morning. | A gull stood on my boot and looked at me. Bold as #mud#. | I hate #gulls#. Loud, greedy, no shame.
b : #bc_every_day# | Bold as a gull, they say. | Loud, like some folk.
a : Every day, #oath#. | They say right. #bc_true# | I'm not greedy, #address#.

scene ivar_rooks
when topic=animals|pastimes here.region=fens here.outdoors=clear|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : See #rooks#? #wager.capitalize# the one on the end goes first. | I count #rooks# every morning. Forty-one today. | Starlings went over in a cloud. #wager.capitalize# you can't count them.
b : Which end? | Why count them? | No.
a : Left. Watch. There! Pay up. #oath#. | Habit. #bc_somebody_has_to# | Nobody can. That's the point.

scene ivar_work_haul
when topic=work self.job=fisher|sailor|none self.workplace
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hauled at #self.workplace# since before light. #wager.capitalize# I hauled more than anyone. | Rope burn. Both paws #hurt#. Don't look. | Told the skipper I'd have the hold clear by noon. #wager.capitalize#. Lost by a hair.
b : Rest them. | That looks sore. | How much?
a : Rest's for #toffs#. | It's nothing. | Never mind how much.

scene ivar_work_pay
when topic=work self.wealth=poor|destitute self.job=fisher|sailor|none
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #wages.capitalize# came in short again. Short, every week. | I'd do better on #odds# than hauling. Some weeks I do. | Haul all day for a crust of #money#. Somebody's eating well off it.
b : That's #bad#. | You'd lose it all. | #bc_true#
a : That's #work#. | Not all of it. Some. | Not me, #address#.

scene ivar_work_skipper
when topic=work self.job=fisher|sailor|none self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and me have #wager# on who's first to the boat. I'm always first. | Told #self.friend# the bar had shifted. Didn't believe me. Bet on it. Won. #oath#. | #self.friend# owes me two coppers and #tart#. I'm counting.
b : Friendly, then. | #bc_clever# | You count everything.
a : Friendly enough. | Not clever. I watch. | I do. #bc_somebody_has_to#

scene ivar_tart
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #tart.capitalize#. Do you know where I'd get one? Somebody's baking. | Won #tart# off a bet last week. Best tart I ever ate. | I'd trade a day's pay for #tart#. Don't tell anyone.
b : The store, maybe. | What was the bet? | Not a word.
a : Store's dear. #shop_dear# | Never you mind. | #good.capitalize#. You'd tell, though. Folk do.

scene ivar_eel
when topic=food self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Eel again. #odds.capitalize# it's eel tomorrow too. | Bread and dripping. It fills a hole when you're #hungry#. | Supper's whatever's left when six of us have been at the pot.
b : Eel's #good#. | It does fill. | #bc_poor_soul#
a : Eel's eel. #saying.capitalize#. | Holes need filling. | Don't pity me. I eat, #address#.

scene ivar_straw
when topic=home here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Put #straw# today. The whole house smells of it. Lovely. | It's #snoring# at mine. I sleep with one ear open. | Somebody tracked #mud# through my straw. I know who. Not saying.
b : That's a #good# smell. | Sounds loud. | Who?
a : Best smell there is, after #warmrain#. | Loud. You get used to #snoring#. | Not saying, I said.

scene ivar_coat
when topic=smalltalk|health here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look at #coat#. Not a speck. That's an hour's brushing. | #mud.capitalize#'s on everyone but me. You'd wonder how. | Somebody brushed past me on the boards with #mud# to the knee. My coat!
b : Very clean. | How, then? | #bc_bad_luck#
a : #bc_always_is# | I watch where I step. And who. | #bad.capitalize# luck for them, if I find them.

scene ivar_road
when topic=smalltalk|travel here.region=fens
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch #road#. Always have. You never know what's coming down it. | Somebody came in down #road# last night. Never saw them leave. | Bet you can't tell me who that was on #road# this morning.
b : What are you watching for? | Who was it? | I can't.
a : Nothing. Everything. Leave it. | Don't know. #uneasy.capitalize#. | No, nor me. That's the trouble.

scene ivar_strangers
when topic=newcomer|smalltalk pair.band=strangers
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : You're new. Which way did you come, #road#? | Don't take this wrong, but I keep my door shut. | Folk come over the causeway every week now. #wager.capitalize# half of them leave.
b : The coast road. | That's fair. | Maybe they will.
a : Hm. #far.capitalize#. Why? | Fair's what it is. | They do. #bc_mostly#

scene ivar_haggle
when topic=prices|smalltalk
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I can't abide #haggle#. Say a price. I'll pay it or I won't. | Stood at the store while two of them were at #haggle# for half an hour. | Bread's up again. #wager.capitalize# it's up next week too.
b : Some like it. | Who won? | #bc_they_always_do#
a : Then they can have it. | The penny. Nobody else. | #bc_always_is#

scene ivar_festival
when topic=festival|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Festival! Races on the boards. I've #wager# on every one. | Last festival I won six coppers on a punt race at #odds#. Six! | Dice at the Heron all night. #wager.capitalize# I'm last to leave.
b : Lose any? | What did you do with it? | #bc_i_might#
a : A few. Never say how many. | #tart.capitalize#. And another. | Come. Bring #money#.

scene ivar_lights
when topic=lore here.region=fens here.time=dusk|night
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : #wager.capitalize# nobody'll walk out to the lights tonight. Nobody ever does. | I counted the lights once. Seven. Then eight. Then three. #oath#. | Folk lay #wager# on the lights at the Heron. How many, how long.
b : Would you? | They move. | #bc_clever#
a : Not for any #money#. | They do. That's why I lost. | Not clever. Patient.

scene ivar_houses
when topic=smalltalk|times pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Asked at a House gate for a bench once. Never again. #toffs.capitalize#. | Bread's up and #wages#'s not. Harder every week. | Nobody up there notices. #odds.capitalize# they never will.
b : What did they say? | It is. | #bc_true#
a : Nothing. That's what they said. | #bc_it_is# | True, sure as mud.

scene ivar_season
when topic=season here.season=winter here.region=fens
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Winter. I don't like winter. Never have. | Ice on the lode. #wager.capitalize# it's thick by the week's end. | Long nights. I watch #road# more in winter.
b : It passes. | #bc_we_will_see# | Why?
a : It does. Not soon enough. | #bc_we_will# | No reason. Habit.

story ivar_hard_winter [topic=family self.age>=30]
  : There was a hard winter when I was young. #cold.capitalize#, and harder than any since.
  : My brother went out along #road# for help. Didn't come back.
  b : I'm sorry.
  : I watch #road# still. I know. I know it's daft.
  b[friends] : It's not daft.
  b : #bc_poor_soul#

story ivar_coat_wager [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I lost #coat# on a wager once. Off my back. Bet I could cross the lode on the ice.
  : I nearly did. Last stride went through.
  ask : What happened?
  b : Ha. Then what?
  : Won it back next week, with interest. Kept #coat# clean since. Every day.
  b : #bc_ha#

story ivar_big_win [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : Biggest win I ever had, I bet a week's #wages# the heron at the weir wouldn't move till noon.
  : Stood there all morning watching it. So did half the hamlet.
  b : Did it move?
  : Five past. Five past noon. I won. #oath#.
  b : #bc_clever#

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. Don't know your face. Where've you come from, and what's it to me?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#! #wager.capitalize# you want something. Am I right?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary] : #greet#. I'm watching you, mind. Nothing personal. I watch everyone.
dlg @1 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I haul, I coil, I bail. #wages.capitalize#'s bad. I make it up on wagers.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : News? Somebody came over #road# last night. Never saw them leave. That's my news.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. #wager.capitalize# I see you before the week's out.
graft resident.hub
choice Fancy a wager? -> ivar_bet
node ivar_bet
say Do I? #oath#! What on? No, I'll pick. #wager.capitalize# the next wolf over the causeway's a stranger.
mood keen
free
choice You're on. -> ivar_bet_on
choice Not today. -> hub
node ivar_bet_on
say Good! We'll watch #road#. Don't you leave before we know. And no cheating, I'll see.
choice Deal. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
